  "mechanism_class": "structural",
  "mechanism_rationale": "In rhbi-v10 (readout-a3aa33cc909a1545b2341f1c), 15/16 executed Tier 1 tasks passed cleanly and model_ae_gan_multimodal satisfied all 8 final metric bounds at step 1200 (precision=0.9431 >= 0.90, component_center_rms_sigma=0.9560 <= 1.0), but over-amplified valley 96th-quantile precision gain (rhbi_tail_spill_gain=1.8) kept thermal scale s_t warm against uncooled autoencoder reconstruction gradients through step 1000 (component_center_rms_sigma=1.0017), shortening its terminal stability suffix to 4/5. Moderating rhbi_tail_spill_gain to 0.95 restores early post-acquisition thermal lock on model_ae_gan_multimodal while still delaying premature cooling on vector_anisotropic long enough for the residual ~7.4% inter-mode bridge particles to clear into the three rotated Gaussian components, paired with unchanged wide-span H_0-connected macro-simplicial settling (rhbi_simplex_macro_settle=true) for interp_saddle_barycentric.",
